  "which roles fit his experience, and what work supports that fit?": {
    "answer": "He was an AI Engineer (RA) at Boston University, Questrom Computational Lab, where he built a document intelligence assistant on Azure for Sikich, an enterprise consulting firm, owned from ingestion through deployment: a LangGraph agent exposing 14 tools for document question answering, cross-document comparison and template-driven generation, grounded by hybrid BM25 and vector retrieval with Cohere re-ranking, guarded by PII and entity redaction, and scored for hallucination rate by LLM-as-a-Judge evaluations. He also led the entire backend for EST's field-service platform, and the part he architected that matters most is scheduling: technicians make recurring visits to many sites for many clients, so the system has to decide who goes where and when, every time.",
